<div class="section" id="life">
    <h2>Life</h2>
    <img src="C:\Users\CCLab\Pictures\lata_mangeshkar.jpg">
    <p>Lata Mangeshkar was an iconic Indian playback singer whose career spanned seven decades, earning her the title of "Queen of Melody" for her unparalleled contribution to Indian music.</p>
</div>

<div class="section" id="works">
    <h2>Works</h2>
    <p>Musical Mastery - She recorded thousands of songs in over thirty-six Indian languages and few foreign languages, becoming the voice of generations.</p>
    <p>Patriotic Influence - Her rendition of "Aye Mere Watan Ke Logo" famously moved Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru to tears and became a symbol of national pride.</p>
    <p>Global Recognition - She was the first Indian to perform at the Royal Albert Hall in London and received the Bharat Ratna, India's highest civilian honor.</p>
</div>

<div class="section" id="legacy">
    <h2>Legacy</h2>
    <p>Lata Mangeshkar's legacy lives on through her timeless voice, which remains the gold standard for playback singing and an inspiration to aspiring musicians worldwide.</p>
